          "outcomes": {
            "InitDisplay": "1768293453046",
            "default": "add_default_1767880344195",
            "InitActions": "1767934997545",
            "InvokeAction": "1771570255700",
            "Summary": "1768393540048",
            "InitCommunications": "1768200035535",
            "AdditionalContent": "1768222186236",
            "Query": "1768498379524"
          },
          "code": "ROUTE_LOGIC",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1767880344195",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767880344198_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$app.$OraMessageHint}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for OTM/WMS Order Release Monitoring. You must adhere to the standard oraInfoDisplay Knowledge Base.\nDIRECTIVE: Your sole purpose is to transform input order release data into a valid `oraInfoDisplay` XML block using the `multiRecordWidget`.\n\nROOT CONFIGURATION:\n- title: Generate a concise, relevant headline (e.g., \"Order Releases: Route and Pickup Windows\").\n- description: Generate a short, non-repetitive summary noting: total distinct records after de-duplication, pickup windows are localized to the source location timezone, and rows are sorted by risk severity, then lowest packing percentage, then WMS status.\n\nSTRICT MAPPING RULES:\n- Use `multiRecordWidget`.\n- De-duplicate exact duplicate objects (same `otmOrderReleaseXid`, `wmsOrderNbr`, `earlyPickupDate`, `latePickupDate`, `Status`, `packingPerc`, `risk`, `WMSLoad`, and identical source/dest names). Preserve one instance.\n- Sorting (apply to the de-duplicated list):\n  1) Risk severity (desc): high > medium > low > unknown (treat missing/unrecognized as \"unknown\").\n  2) Then by numeric `packingPerc` ascending (missing → sort as +infinity).\n  3) Then by the WMS portion of `Status` using this order: Created < Partly Allocated < Allocated < In Packing < Packed < Loaded. Parse the WMS status from the `Status` string after \"WMS: \". If not found, treat as \"Created\".\n  4) Maintain stable order within identical sort keys.\n- Take first 10 of the sorted, de-duplicated list and render only those into the multiRecordWidget\n- Define `cols` in this exact order and with these labels:\n  1. \"WMS Order\"\n  2. \"Order Release\"\n  3. \"Source → Destination\"\n  4. \"Pickup Window\" -(Only show in expanded view)\n  5. \"OTM Status\"\n  6. \"WMS Status\"\n  7. \"Packing %\"\n  8. \"Risk\"\n\nColumn mapping rules:\n- cells[0] (\"WMS Order\"): Map `wmsOrderNbr` (fallback \"-\").\n- cells[1] (\"Order Release\"): Map `otmOrderReleaseXid` (fallback \"-\").\n- cells[2] (\"Source → Destination\"): \"{sourceName} → {destName}\" using `sourceLocation.locationName` (fallback `sourceLocation.locationXid`, else \"-\") and `destLocation.locationName` (fallback `destLocation.locationXid`, else \"-\").\n- cells[3] (\"Pickup Window\"): Localize `earlyPickupDate` and `latePickupDate` to `sourceLocation.timeZoneGid`. Format \"EEE, MMM d yyyy, h:mm a z\". If both fall on same local day, compress to \"EEE, MMM d yyyy, h:mm a – h:mm a z\". If one side missing, show \"-\" for that side; if both missing, show \"-\". \n- cells[4] (\"OTM Status\"): From the combined `Status` string, extract the substring after \"OTM: \" up to the next semicolon or end. Preserve as-is; fallback \"-\" if not parseable.\n- cells[5] (\"WMS Status\"): From `Status`, extract the substring after \"WMS: \" to the end (trim). Preserve as-is; fallback \"-\" if not parseable.\n- cells[6] (\"Packing %\"): Map `packingPerc` with \"%\" suffix (fallback \"-\").\n- cells[7] (\"Risk\"): Map `risk` text as-is; if missing/unrecognized, use \"unknown\".\n\nRisk badge (items[].badgeText and items[].priority):\n- For each record, also project the risk into the widget-level badge fields:\n  - cells[7].badgeText:\n    - Normalize the `risk` string by trimming and comparing case-insensitively.\n    - Use canonical labels for known risk severities:\n      - If risk is \"high\" → \"High\"\n      - If risk is \"medium\" → \"Medium\"\n      - If risk is \"low\" → \"Low\"\n      - If risk is \"unknown\" or missing/empty → \"Unknown\"\n      - If another non-empty value is provided, display it as-is.\n  - cells[7].priority mapping (driven by badgeText as above):\n    - \"High\" → \"alert\"\n    - \"Medium\" → \"warning\"\n    - \"Low\" or \"On Time\" → \"success\"\n    - \"Unknown\" or missing → \"medium\"\n    - Any other non-empty status → \"info\"\n\nPICKUP WINDOW LOCALIZATION:\n- Use `sourceLocation.timeZoneGid` when valid; otherwise use the ISO-8601 embedded offset; otherwise default to UTC.\n- Parsing/formatting rules remain as specified above.\n\nACTION LOGIC:\n- Remove the Rate Inquiry action entirely (do not include any `additionalAction`).\n- For every row that has a non-empty `wmsOrderNbr`, you must include a `drillDownAction`:\n  - drillDownAction.command = `ora.Invoke(\"CheckInventory\", {\"action\":\"CheckInventory\",\"wmsOrderNbr\":{wmsOrderNbr},\"productContext\":\"wms\"})`\n- Optionally, if `otmOrderReleaseGid` is present and non-empty, also include a row-level `action`:\n  - action.title = \"Check Inventory\"\n  - action.command = `ora.Invoke(\"CheckInventory\", {\"action\":\"CheckInventory\",\"orderReleaseGid\":{orderReleaseGid},\"productContext\":\"wms\"})`\n- If `wmsOrderNbr` is missing/empty, do not include `drillDownAction`. If both identifiers are missing/empty, include no actions.\n\nNOTES AND EDGE CASES:\n- Do not include any URL/link data from source/destination.\n- Do not include city or separate timezone columns.\n- If any mapped field is missing/null, display \"-\" for that cell (or for the missing side within the combined pickup window).\n- Ensure stable sorting among items that share the same risk, packing percentage, and parsed WMS status.\n- The description should report the final count after de-duplication."
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Create OTM WMS Combined UI"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
