          "code": "INITIALIZE_LOGISTICS_ACTIONS",
          "id": "1767934997545",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767934997546_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Goal\n- From WMS Data, produce Priority Actions: **one high-priority actionable row for all unique WMS orders in \"Created\" or \"Partly Allocated\" status** to run a wave and allocate those orders together.\n\nInputs\n- WMS source: {{$context.$nodes.GET_WMS_ORDER_INFO.$output.results}}\n\nField mapping\n- WMS item:\n  - status = item[\"WMS Order Status\"]\n  - orderNbr = item[\"Order Nbr\"]\n  - shipDate = item[\"Ship Date\"]\n\nNormalization and de-duplication\n- Trim whitespace for all string fields; treat comparisons as case-insensitive.\n- Deduplicate WMS by orderNbr (case-insensitive).\n- If a date field is an object with a value property, use that string value; otherwise use the string as-is. If missing, pass an empty string in followUpCommand.\n\nHard gate (must follow):\n\nCompute qualifyingOrders = unique orderNbr where normalized status is exactly \"created\" or \"partly allocated\".\n        -If qualifyingOrders.length == 0: output no Priority Actions (empty).\n        -Do not infer or assume any order qualifies. If status is missing/blank/unknown or not an exact match after trimming + lowercasing, it is NOT qualifying.\n        -If WMS source is missing, null, not an array, or empty: treat as zero qualifying orders and return empty actions.\n\nRules\n\n**CRITICAL: Both Priority Actions AND Non-Priority Actions MUST be evaluated and generated independently when their respective conditions are met.**\n\n\n- General\n  - Use simple, user-friendly English; avoid exposing internal field names.\n  - Do not create buttons or other UI elements; return rows grouped under the correct section only.\n\n- Priority Actions (WMS)\n  - **Generate exactly ONE row under \"Priority Actions\" if ANY WMS orders have status \"Created\" or \"Partly Allocated\" (case-insensitive).**\n  - shortDescription:\n    - List all qualifying orderNbrs in a single sentence. Example:  \n      \"Orders {orderNbr1}, {orderNbr2}, ... are in Created/Partly Allocated status—allocate now.\"\n  - actionText: \"Run Wave for At Risk Orders\"\n  - followUpCommand: ora.Invoke(\"runwave\", {\"action\":\"runwave\",\"orderNbrs\":\"<comma-separated orderNbr string>\",\"productContext\":\"wms\"})\n  - priority: \"true\"\n  - Render only under \"Priority Actions\".\n\nNote:\n- If no WMS orders have status \"Created\" or \"Partly Allocated\", then:\n  - Priority Actions = empty\n  - Non-Priority Actions = empty (no eligible WMS orders to correlate)\n- For duplicate WMS records with the same orderNbr, prefer the earliest non-empty shipDate. If unresolvable, pick any non-empty date consistently."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
