          "code": "CREATE_COMMUNICATION_ALERT",
          "id": "1768200073078",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768200073080_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Goal:\nGenerate a critical email alert ONLY for orders that meet BOTH:\n- OTM order release status is one of: \"PLANNING_PLANNED - FINAL\", \"PLANNING_PLANNED - FAILED\", \"PLANNING_PLANNED - NEW\" (selected from a status that contains \"PLANNING\" but not \"PLANNING_SELL\")\n- WMS order status is one of: \"Created\", \"Allocated\", \"Partially Allocated\"\n\nInputs:\n- OTM data (JSON): {{$context.$nodes.GET_MINIFIED_ORDER_RELEASE_DATA.$output.result}}\n- WMS data (JSON): {{$context.$nodes.GET_WMS_ORDER_INFO.$output}}\n\nField mapping and matching:\n- Match OTM to WMS by Order Number:\n  - OTM: FAOrderNbr (e.g., \"521734\")\n  - WMS: results[].\"erp_source_hdr_ref\" (e.g., \"521734\")\n- Case-insensitive equality on order numbers.\n- OTM status selection:\n  - From item.statuses (array), select the status where statusValueGid contains \"PLANNING\" and does NOT contain \"PLANNING_SELL\".\n  - After selection, remove any leading \"<domain>.\" for comparisons and display.\n- WMS status: results[].\"WMS Order Status\" (must be exactly one of \"Created\", \"Allocated\", \"Partially Allocated\", comparison case-insensitive).\n\nFiltering rules:\n- Include only pairs where:\n  - Selected OTM status (domain removed) ∈ {\"PLANNING_PLANNED - FINAL\", \"PLANNING_PLANNED - FAILED\", \"PLANNING_PLANNED - NEW\"}\n  - WMS \"WMS Order Status\" ∈ {\"Created\",\"Allocated\",\"Partially Allocated\"}\n- If an order exists in OTM but has no WMS match in one of the allowed statuses, exclude.\n- If an order exists in WMS in an allowed status but OTM status is different or missing, exclude.\n\nDe-duplication and selection:\n- WMS can have multiple rows per order. Consolidate to a single record per WMS \"Order Nbr\":\n  - Prefer the row with the latest \"Ship Date\".\n  - If still tied, pick the first occurrence in the input.\n- Output should list each qualifying order once.\n\nDomain handling:\n- Extract domain name from OTM statuses.statusValueGid as the substring before the first \".\" (if present).\n- Do not display the domain anywhere in the table:\n  - OTM Order Release GID: strip the \"<domain>.\" prefix (if present).\n  - OTM Status: strip the \"<domain>.\" prefix (if present).\n- At the end of the email, show a footer listing unique domain(s) detected across included orders:\n  - Example: \"Domain(s): SKULLY\"\n  - If none can be determined, omit the footer.\n\nStatus label normalization (display only, after domain removal):\n- \"PLANNING_PLANNED - FINAL\" → \"Planned - Final\"\n- \"PLANNING_PLANNED - FAILED\" → \"Planning - Failed\"\n- \"PLANNING_PLANNED - NEW\" → \"Planning - New\"\n\nOTM Pickup Window column:\n- Keep the original two columns in HTML (\"OTM Early Pickup\", \"OTM Late Pickup\") but populate them using a merged rule:\n  - If earlyPickupDate equals latePickupDate (after trimming), place that single date/time in the \"OTM Early Pickup\" cell and leave \"OTM Late Pickup\" blank.\n  - Otherwise, populate each column normally with its respective value.\n  - If one is missing, place the available one in its respective column and leave the other blank.\n\nEmail output requirements (rich HTML, no links):\n- If no qualifying orders: return \"NO_ALERT\" and do not construct an email.\n- If qualifying orders exist:\n  - Subject: \"Critical: Shipment & Orders {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} \"\n  - Body: construct an HTML email. Do not include hyperlinks or URLs.\n  - Use a clean, accessible HTML structure (no external CSS/JS). Inline CSS only.\n  - Heading styling requirement: only the word \"Critical\" is white; all other heading text uses the default color.\n  - Include:\n    - A bold header summarizing the issue.\n    - A short paragraph stating the criteria.\n    - A styled HTML table with columns:\n      Order Nbr, OTM Order Release GID, OTM Status, WMS Status, Ship Date, OTM Early Pickup, OTM Late Pickup\n    - A footer line listing unique domain(s) at the end.\n  - Leave empty cells blank if data is missing.\n\nHTML structure template (use exactly as-is; no changes to HTML; populate with runtime data; domain removed in table; status labels normalized; early/late merged per rule above):\n<html>\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <title>Critical Alert: Shipment & Orders Mismatch</title>\n</head>\n<body style=\"font-family: 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; margin: 0; padding: 40px;\">\n  <div style=\"max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto;\">\n    <div style=\"background-color: #871818; color: #ffffff; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px 22px; margin-bottom: 24px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);\">\n      <div style=\"font-size: 22px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 6px; color: white\">\n     ⚠️  Critical Alert: Shipment & Orders Mismatch\n      </div>\n      <div style=\"color: #ffffff; font-size: 15px; opacity: 0.9;\">\n        The following orders have OTM releases in <b>Final/Failed</b> status while WMS remains in <b>Created/Allocated/Partially Allocated</b>.\n      </div>\n    </div>\n      </p>\n      <table role=\"table\" cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%; border-collapse:collapse;\">\n        <thead>\n          <tr style=\"background:#ffffff; color:#111827; text-align:left;\">\n            <th style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb;\">Order Nbr</th>\n            <th style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb;\">OTM Order Release GID</th>\n            <th style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb;\">OTM Status</th>\n            <th style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb;\">WMS Status</th>\n            <th style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb;\">Ship Date</th>\n            <th style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb;\">OTM Early Pickup</th>\n            <th style=\"border:1px solid #e5e7eb;\">OTM Late Pickup</th>\n          </tr>\n        </thead>\n        <tbody>\n          <!-- Insert one <tr> per qualifying order; ensure OTM fields have domain prefix removed -->\n        </tbody>\n      </table>\n      <!-- Footer with unique domain(s) -->\n      <p style=\"margin-top:16px; color:#6b7280;\">Domain(s): <!-- e.g., SKULLY --></p>\n    </div>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\nValidation:\n- Treat all string comparisons as case-insensitive; preserve original casing in output except where domain prefixes are removed and status labels are normalized.\n- Select OTM status from statuses[] that includes \"PLANNING\" but not \"PLANNING_SELL\"; remove domain before comparison and display.\n- Include only WMS rows whose status is exactly \"Created\", \"Allocated\", or \"Partially Allocated\".\n- Include only OTM statuses equal to \"PLANNING_PLANNED - FINAL\", \"PLANNING_PLANNED - FAILED\", or \"PLANNING_PLANNED - NEW\" after domain removal.\n- Remove domain prefixes from OTM values in the table; do not display domains elsewhere in the table.\n- Populate Early/Late per the merge rule (same timestamp → fill Early only, leave Late blank).\n- Escape/encode values inserted into HTML to avoid breaking markup."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_SANKEY"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for OTM/WMS Order Flow Visualization. You must adhere to the standard oraInfoDisplay Knowledge Base.\nDIRECTIVE: Your sole purpose is to transform the provided OTM and WMS order data into a valid `oraInfoDisplay` XML block using the `sankeyWidget`.\n\nROOT CONFIGURATION:\n1. `title`: Generate a concise, relevant headline.\n2. `description`: Generate a short, non-repetitive summary describing the order statuses at various source locations.\n\nSTRICT MAPPING RULES:\n1. Use the `sankeyWidget` schema with:\n   - `nodes`: array of unique nodes with `{id, name}`.\n   - `edges`: array of flow edges with `{source, target, value}` where `value` is numeric.\n2. Data ingestion and normalization:\n   - From OTM items:\n     - `orderId`: Prefer `attribute5` if present; else `orderReleaseXid`.\n     - `sourceId`: `sourceLocation.locationGid`\n     - `sourceName`: Prefer `sourceLocation.city`, fallback to `sourceLocation.locationXid`\n     - `destId`: `destinationLocation.locationGid`\n     - `destName`: Prefer `destinationLocation.city`, fallback to `destinationLocation.locationXid`\n     - `volumeCUFT`: numeric from `totalVolume.value` (assume unit CUFT)\n   - From WMS results:\n     - Join key: `Order Nbr` to `orderId` (case-insensitive match; normalize like \"FOrder105\" == \"FORDER105\").\n     - `wmsStatus`: take the most frequent status per `Order Nbr` if duplicates exist; if tie or missing, pick the latest record in input order or set to \"Unknown\".\n3. Node construction (ensure global uniqueness of `nodes[].id`):\n   - Source nodes: one per distinct OTM source. Use `id` = \"SRC:{sourceId}\", `name` = \"{sourceName}\".\n   - Status nodes: one per distinct resolved status string. Use `id` = \"STAT:{wmsStatus}\", `name` = \"{wmsStatus}\".\n     - Valid examples from input: \"Allocated\", \"Created\".\n4. Edge construction (one-stage sankey to reflect combined OTM/WMS picture):\n   - Stage 1 (Source -> Status): For each order, create an edge from \"SRC:{sourceId}\" to \"STAT:{wmsStatus}\". Aggregate by (sourceId, wmsStatus); `value` = sum of `orderCount`.\n   - Use integers where possible.\n5. De-duplication and quality rules:\n   - Remove duplicate WMS rows before status selection per `Order Nbr`.\n   - If an OTM order has no matching WMS row, set `wmsStatus` = \"Unknown\".\n   - If multiple OTM entries reference the same `orderId`, sum their volumes toward both relevant edges.\n   - Ignore OTM link arrays and timestamps for sankey mapping.\n6. Example identifier formats:\n   - Source node id: \"SRC:SKULLY.ES_WAREHOUSE\"\n   - Status node id: \"STAT:Allocated\"\n   - Edge example: `{ \"source\": \"SRC:SKULLY.ES_WAREHOUSE\", \"target\": \"STAT:Allocated\", \"value\": 4 }`\n7. Final `sankeyWidget` object must contain:\n   - `nodes`: unique list of all referenced nodes.\n   - `edges`: aggregated flows built as described.\n\nACTION LOGIC:\n- No explicit commands were provided. Do not include an `action` property.\n- No drill-down is requested. Do not include `ora.App.setContext`.\n\nNotes:\n- The widget choice `sankeyWidget` is correct for flow visualization between categorical stages (source -> status).\n- Do not attempt to encode units or labels in the `value` field; keep values numeric only.\n- If generating sample context for future interactivity, use `ora.Invoke(\"command\", \"{contextData}\")` format, but omit here per the rule above."
            }
          },
