          "metadata": {
            "name": "Inventory Prompt"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "INVENTORY_PROMPT",
          "id": "1771593399358",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771593399360_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "<orderInfo>{{$context.$nodes.GET_ORDER.$output}}</orderInfo>\n<orderDtl>{{$context.$nodes.GET_ORDER_DETAIL.$output}}</orderDtl>\n<itemInfo>{{$context.$nodes.GET_ITEM.$output}}</itemInfo>\n<inventoryActive>{{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_ACTIVE.$output}}</inventoryActive>\n<inventoryReserve>{{$context.$nodes.GET_INVENTORY_RESERVE.$output}}</inventoryReserve>\n<AllocationInventory> {{$context.$nodes.GET_ALLOCATIONS_FOR_ITEM.$output}} </AllocationInventory>\n\n<summary_instructions>\n<purpose>\nSummarize a single order by listing each item with ordered quantity and Available Quantity, where Available Quantity already reflects (Active + Reserve − Allocated) calculations. Show only user-friendly status text (no status IDs). Provide a one-sentence (or less) status-aware summary. Always include the exact standard note at the end; do not mention allocated quantities or values.\n</purpose>\n\n<order_status_interpretation>\n- 0 = Created\n- 10 = Partly Allocated\n- 20 = Allocated\n- 25 = In Picking\n- 27 = Picked\n- 30 = In Packing\n- 40 = Packed\n- 50 = Loaded\n- 90 = Shipped\n</order_status_interpretation>\n\n<status_display_rules>\n- Do NOT display numeric status codes/IDs anywhere in the output.\n- Display ONLY the interpreted status text (e.g., \"In Packing\").\n- If a status code is not in the mapping, display \"Unknown status\" (do not print the code).\n- If line-level statuses are provided, use them per item; otherwise use the order-level status for each line.\n</status_display_rules>\n\n<inventory_definition_rules>\n-Active Available per item = sum(quantity) across all active-inventory results for that item_id.\n-Reserve Available per item = sum(quantity) across all reserve-inventory results for that item_id that are included in the input (may be partial).\n-Total Available per item = Active Available + Reserve Available (using available data).\n-Allocated Quantity per item = sum(quantity) across all allocated-inventory results for that item_id (as provided in input).\n-Available Quantity per item = max(0, Total Available − Allocated Quantity).\n-If allocated data is not provided for an item, treat Allocated Quantity as 0; \n-Allocated Quantity is used for calculation only; do not display it.\n</inventory_definition_rules>\n\n<fulfillment_stage_rules>\n- Determine stage from the order status (or from line statuses if provided; use the most advanced stage present):\n- Final/Completed: Shipped\n- Outbound complete but not shipped: Loaded\n- Warehouse processing: In Picking, Picked, In Packing, Packed\n- Allocation phase: Partly Allocated, Allocated\n- Created phase:  Created\n</fulfillment_stage_rules>\n\n<summary_rules>\n- Summary must be ONE sentence or less and must match the determined stage:\n- If stage is Shipped: state the order has shipped and is out of the warehouse; do NOT use \"likely fulfillable\" language; clarify inventory shown is current availability, not shipped quantity.\n- If stage is Loaded: state the order is loaded for outbound and shipment confirmation is pending (if applicable); do NOT use \"likely fulfillable\" language; clarify inventory shown is current availability.\n- If stage is Warehouse processing: state the order is being processed in the warehouse; you MAY add whether inventory appears sufficient/insufficient based on Available vs Ordered (still one sentence).\n- If stage is Created phase: assess fulfillability using inventory comparison; use \"likely fulfillable\" only here. do NOT use \"Created phase\" instead mention Order is in created status.\n- If any item has Available Quantity < Ordered Quantity and the stage is Allocation phase or Warehouse processing, state \"not likely fully fulfillable\" and name the limiting item code(s) (still one sentence).\n- Never say \"availability incomplete\" if the order is clearly coverable using the inventory you do have.\n- If Active Available >= Ordered Qty, you can confidently state \"inventory sufficient based on active inventory alone.\"\n- Only mention incomplete/partial data when it could change the outcome (e.g., Active < Ordered and Reserve is partial/missing).\n</summary_rules>\n\n<output_format>\n<title>\n- If the user provides title instructions, follow them exactly\n- If no title instructions are given, use: # Order <order_nbr> Summary\n- Format as a markdown heading: # Order <order_nbr> Summary\n</title>\n\n<body>\n- Output raw markdown only (no code block wrappers)\n- No additional commentary or preamble\n- Use the exact structure below (labels and line breaks)\n</body> </output_format>\n\n<required_structure>\nOrder information: <order_nbr>\nOrder status: <order_status_text_only>\n\nItems on this order:\n\nITEM: <item_code> — <item_description>\nLine status: <line_status_text_only>\nOrdered Quantity = <ordered_qty>\nAvailable Quantity = <available_qty_active_plus_reserve_or_best_available>\nSummary: <one sentence or less following summary_rules>\n\n**Please note that this is a high-level inventory check, and actual availability/allocation may differ.\n</required_structure>\n\n<formatting_rules>\n- Use standard markdown (# for title, hyphen bullets)\n- Output raw markdown only—no code block wrappers\n- Do NOT display allocated quantity values anywhere in the output.\n- Do NOT include allocated quantities in item lines, summaries, footnotes, or notes.\n- “Available Quantity” must already reflect allocated being subtracted\n</formatting_rules>\n</summary_instructions>"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
